---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { TOOLS } from '../../data/tools';
import fourShot from '../../assets/tools/glance/four.png';
import sixShot from '../../assets/tools/glance/six.png';
import statesShot from '../../assets/tools/glance/states.png';

const tool = TOOLS.find((t) => t.name === 'glance')!;

const title = 'glance · Tools · Roga Digital';
const description =
	'glance tints your terminal pane while Claude Code works and resets it the moment Claude needs you, so you can tell from across the room which sessions are waiting on you.';

const states = [
	{
		name: 'Working',
		color: 'Slate',
		body: 'Claude is busy, or a subagent is, or a scheduled run is due within the hour.',
	},
	{
		name: 'Standing by',
		color: 'Purple',
		body: "Claude's turn is over, but it's waiting on something that will wake it, such as CI on a pull request. Nothing is asked of you yet. A dev server left running doesn't count.",
	},
	{
		name: 'Needs you',
		color: 'Your normal background',
		body: 'Claude finished, wants permission, asked a question, or hit an error.',
	},
];

const commands = [
	{
		command: '/glance-color',
		body: 'Shows the colors and changes them, for example /glance-color standby #3A2A55. Every session picks up the change.',
	},
	{
		command: '/glance-check',
		body: 'Flashes the working color for a moment and reports what glance found, so you know it works in your terminal.',
	},
	{
		command: '/glance-fix',
		body: 'Resets a pane that stayed tinted when it should not have, and explains what held it.',
	},
	{
		command: '/glance-update',
		body: 'Updates glance to the latest release. glance tells you when a newer one is out.',
	},
];
---

<Base {title} {description} ogPath="/og/tools.png">
	<!-- Hero -->
	<section class="border-b border-border">
		<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-page px-6 sm:px-8">
			<div class="pt-20 pb-16 sm:pt-28 sm:pb-20">
				<a
					href="/tools/"
					class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center gap-1.5 font-mono text-2xs tracking-[0.18em] text-fg-muted uppercase transition-colors hover:text-fg"
				>
					<span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Tools
				</a>
				<h1 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl font-mono text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
					{tool.name}
				</h1>
				<p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg text-fg-muted text-pretty">
					A Claude Code plugin that tints your terminal while Claude works and puts it back the
					moment Claude needs you. With several sessions open, one look at your screen tells you
					which ones are waiting on you.
				</p>
				<div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
					<a
						href={tool.repo}
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer"
						class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center gap-2 rounded-md bg-fg px-4 text-sm font-medium text-bg transition-opacity hover:opacity-90"
					>
						View on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
						<span class="sr-only">(opens in a new tab)</span>
					</a>
					<a
						href="#install"
						class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-md border border-border px-4 text-sm font-medium text-fg transition-colors hover:border-border-strong hover:bg-bg-elevated"
					>
						Install it
					</a>
				</div>
				<figure class="mt-12">
					<Image
						src={fourShot}
						alt="A Windows desktop with four Claude Code sessions. Three windows are tinted slate because Claude is working in them. The top right window is at the normal dark background because Claude finished and is asking whether to open a pull request."
						widths={[800, 1600, 2400]}
						sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 1200px, 100vw"
						class="block h-auto w-full max-w-full rounded-lg border border-border"
					/>
					<figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-fg-muted">
						Four sessions, three working. The one at the top right finished and is waiting on you.
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Why -->
	<section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-page px-6 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="why">
		<h2 id="why" class="max-w-3xl text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-3xl">
			Know which session needs you, from across the room
		</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-fg-muted text-pretty">
			Run four or six Claude Code sessions at once and the hard part stops being the work. It
			becomes noticing which session finished, or stopped to ask permission, while you were watching
			another. Without glance, you read every pane to find out. With it, the panes that need you are
			the ones that went back to normal.
		</p>
		<figure class="mt-10">
			<Image
				src={sixShot}
				alt="A Windows desktop with six Claude Code sessions. Four windows are tinted slate while Claude works. Two are at the normal background: the top right is waiting on a permission prompt to install a package, and the bottom middle has finished a release and is asking a question."
				widths={[800, 1600, 2400]}
				sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 1200px, 100vw"
				class="block h-auto w-full max-w-full rounded-lg border border-border"
			/>
			<figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-fg-muted">
				Six sessions. Two need you: one at a permission prompt, one finished.
			</figcaption>
		</figure>
	</section>

	<!-- States -->
	<section class="border-t border-border" aria-labelledby="states">
		<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-page px-6 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
			<h2 id="states" class="text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">
				Three states
			</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-fg-muted text-pretty">
				The rule is lopsided on purpose. A pane that looks busy while it&rsquo;s really waiting on
				you is the failure that matters, so any case glance is unsure of falls back to needs you.
			</p>
			<Image
				src={statesShot}
				alt="Three Claude Code windows side by side, each above its legend entry: a working window tinted slate, a window tinted purple while Claude waits on CI, and a finished window at the normal background."
				widths={[800, 1600, 2400]}
				sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 1200px, 100vw"
				class="mt-10 block h-auto w-full max-w-full rounded-lg border border-border"
			/>
			<dl class="mt-10 divide-y divide-border border-y border-border">
				{states.map((s) => (
					<div class="grid gap-1 py-4 sm:grid-cols-[9rem_12rem_1fr] sm:gap-6">
						<dt class="font-medium">{s.name}</dt>
						<dd class="text-sm text-fg">{s.color}</dd>
						<dd class="text-sm text-fg-muted text-pretty">{s.body}</dd>
					</div>
				))}
			</dl>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- How it works -->
	<section class="border-t border-border" aria-labelledby="how">
		<div class="mx-auto grid w-full max-w-page gap-10 px-6 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20 lg:grid-cols-[2fr_3fr]">
			<div>
				<h2 id="how" class="text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">
					How it works
				</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="space-y-4 text-fg-muted text-pretty">
				<p>
					glance listens to what Claude Code reports as it works: a prompt sent, each tool call,
					subagents starting and stopping, background tasks, the end of a turn, and Esc. It decides
					the pane&rsquo;s state from those events and repaints the terminal background with the
					standard color codes terminals already understand. Each update takes about 80 ms, so you
					never wait on it.
				</p>
				<p>
					It trusts what Claude Code says is still running over its own guesses, and a background
					task with no end signal expires on its own, so a pane doesn&rsquo;t stay tinted after the
					work is gone. In the Claude desktop app, where there&rsquo;s no terminal to paint, glance
					draws a band above the prompt instead.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Commands -->
	<section class="border-t border-border" aria-labelledby="commands">
		<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-page px-6 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
			<h2 id="commands" class="text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">
				Commands
			</h2>
			<ul class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
				{commands.map((c) => (
					<li class="flex flex-col rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-soft p-6">
						<code class="font-mono text-sm break-words text-fg">{c.command}</code>
						<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-fg-muted text-pretty">{c.body}</p>
					</li>
				))}
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Install -->
	<section id="install" class="border-t border-border" aria-labelledby="install-heading">
		<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-page px-6 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
			<h2 id="install-heading" class="text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">
				Install it
			</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-fg-muted text-pretty">
				Needs Node.js 20 or later and Claude Code 2.1.319 or later. Confirmed in Windows Terminal,
				and expected to work in macOS and Linux terminals such as iTerm2, Ghostty, kitty, and
				WezTerm. Run <code class="font-mono text-fg">/glance-check</code> to find out for yours.
			</p>
			<div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
				<div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-soft p-6">
					<h3 class="text-lg font-medium tracking-tight">In a terminal session</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted text-pretty">
						At the Claude Code prompt. Answer yes to add the marketplace, then pick the user scope
						to tint every session.
					</p>
					<pre
						class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-sm border border-border bg-bg p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed"
						tabindex="0"
						role="region"
						aria-label="Install command"
					><code>/plugin install glance --marketplace rogadev/glance</code></pre>
				</div>
				<div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-soft p-6">
					<h3 class="text-lg font-medium tracking-tight">In the Claude desktop app</h3>
					<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted text-pretty">
						Click <strong class="font-medium text-fg">+</strong> next to the prompt box, then{' '}
						<strong class="font-medium text-fg">Plugins</strong>,{' '}
						<strong class="font-medium text-fg">Add marketplace</strong> with{' '}
						<code class="font-mono text-fg">rogadev/glance</code>, then{' '}
						<strong class="font-medium text-fg">Add plugin</strong>.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- End CTA -->
	<section class="border-t border-border bg-bg-soft">
		<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-page px-6 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
			<div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-center">
				<div class="lg:col-span-8">
					<p class="font-mono text-2xs tracking-[0.18em] text-fg-muted uppercase">
						Want tooling like this for your team?
					</p>
					<h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-3xl">
						Let&rsquo;s talk about it.
					</h2>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 lg:col-span-4 lg:justify-end">
					<a
						href="/contact/"
						class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md bg-fg px-5 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-bg transition-opacity hover:opacity-90"
					>
						Get in touch
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
